=== layout: two-panels

# Competition includes the current solution

@left

## Direct alternative

Another product using a similar approach for the same customer.

@right

## Indirect alternative

A different way to meet the need, including the customer's current practice.

@notes

BioLights discusses other biotechnology lighting companies but discounts conventional
lighting. Ask which alternatives the customer would actually compare at purchase time.
A different technology or country does not automatically remove competition.
Prior Lecture 06D teaching sequence, slide 21: Competition includes the current solution.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Final paragraph claiming no direct competitors and listing alternatives](assets/business_plan_samples/chronic_competition.png)

@caption

No competitors? Read the list. *Chronic excerpt.*

@notes

Ask: what can the customer already do? A different mechanism can still compete for the same purchase.
The filename is dated 2015, while the cover says October 2020; do not infer assignment year from the filename.
Focus on the competition argument, not medical evaluation of the listed treatments.
Source screenshot: 2015-Chronic_Executive_Summary.pdf, PDF page 2; asset chronic_competition.png.
Original source pixels are preserved. Full crop coordinates and hashes: assets/business_plan_samples/sources.json.
