=== layout: one-panel

# Compare on the customer's terms

@body

| Option | Performance | Total cost | Practical limit |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Current practice | Cite a result | State the unit | Identify the burden |
| Named competitor | Cite a result | Use the same unit | Explain the tradeoff |
| Your proposal | State a target | Label the estimate | Name the untested step |

@notes

Fill this table with researched information. Empty template cells are prompts, not facts.
Use comparable conditions, dates, units, and customer groups.
Avoid calling a proposed target a measured advantage.
Prior Lecture 06D teaching sequence, slide 22: Compare on the customer's terms.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Market paragraph for cost-boundary critique](assets/business_plan_samples/aquazyme_market.png)

@caption

Which cost are we counting? *Aquazyme excerpt.*

@notes

The sample compares ocean-cleanup spending with the cost of genetically modifying a microbe.
Keep the original paragraph visible. Ask what is missing from the cost of delivering and operating a complete service.
The numbers are historical student estimates, not current prices or verified cleanup costs.
